00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.200
It's been a long day and I've been working pretty hard

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.520
I'm getting a little tired so I figured I should probably get some coffee

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.800
You may have noticed that your screen is a bit different today

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.360
You're actually watching a 3D, 180 degree VR video

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:25.980
Youtube approached us and asked us if we would be interested in experimenting with a prototype camera to make an entire vlog with

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.880
It was an interesting proposal so we rigged it up to a gimball and tried to see if it was possible

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.480
This is not a sponsored video by the way

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:43.700
You know, I said I was going to get some coffee but really... I just wanted to ride the one-wheel some more

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.900
*spots a gap* ooooohhhh. Let's go through here

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.960
So. I had paint on my hands and took my ring off to wash my hands.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:56.140
I sat on a table in the back prop room and I forgot to put it back on

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.840
and then at some point in the day somebody else knocked it off the table somehow even though we don't use that table that much

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:10.780
and later that evening I realised that I was misisng my ring and I went outside and looked for it. I looked round desks and I couldn't find it

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.520
and I was like... welllll. It might just be gone

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.200
The thing is I'm getting a nicer one to actually wear everyday

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:19.780
uhm

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.700
So, it wasn't like...

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:26.640
the biggest deal in the world. It was gone but it still kinda sucked as it was a sentimental thing

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.700
The tricky thing is to ask yourself. It's a risk or reward scenario.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:39.260
Do I not tell Ivy and hope she doesn't notice and either hope to:

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.960
A) Find the ring (or)
B) buy another ring in time... that I stopped wearing this one

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:46.820
and there by escape unscathed without getting in trouble

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:47.540
or

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:49.980
Do I tell her?

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.460
Get in trouble

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:52.260
but

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:56.620
much less trouble than I would be in if she would find out. Say... a week down the line

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.460
that I lost the ring a week ago and didn't tell her

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:00.320
So it's a really like

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:02.420
it's a really big conundrum

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:03.640
Do I tell her?

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:04.480
Do I don't tell her?

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:05.160
and.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.100
well guys. I'm a risk taker

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.320
So I didn't tell her

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.120
and sure enough this morning

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:13.140
I come in and Carmichael goes 'Hey NIKO! You misisng something?'

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:15.080
... well ... I guess I am. :'(

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.000
and he hands me the ring

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:18.940
and he saves my life

